/-!
# Geroch's theorem for singular flat spacetimes, abstractly — the sorry-free part

`theo:geroch_sing` — `ETT.tex:1771`: here (i)⇒(ii) (`geroch_sing_i_imp_ii`), (i)⇒(iii)
(`geroch_sing_i_imp_iii`) and the splitting (`geroch_sing_split`); its principal statement, the
equivalence `geroch_sing_of_stronglyCausal`, rests on `theo:geroch`'s cited (iii)⇒(i) and lives in
the scaffold remainder `CausalScaffold.SingularGeroch`. `rem:singular_flat_spacetime_therefore` —
`ETT.tex:1508`, principal statement `geroch_hypotheses`. `prop:mesure_admissible` —
`ETT.tex:1726`. `def:singular_spacetime` — `ETT.tex:1500`, abstracted (`SingularFlatSpacetime`).
`lem:cup_cap_BTZ` — `ETT.tex:1825`, its certificate `cupCapBTZAsPrinted_of_globallyHyperbolic`
(DEC-19, on `Causal.SingularFlat`). The author ruled (DEC-18) that `theo:geroch_sing` and
`rem:singular_flat_spacetime_therefore` assume `M` strongly causal; that hypothesis is carried.
None is marked: the model facts are the fields of `SingularFlatAxioms` (`Causal.SingularFlat`),
the local measures in charts are the hypothesis `ModelMeasures`, and the splitting clause is
proved from the flow of `lem:vecteur`, carried as the named hypothesis `VecteurFlow`.

**Split (DEC-78, 2026-11-02).** This module is the sorry-free part of the scaffold file
`scaffold/CausalScaffold/SingularGeroch.lean`, moved here verbatim (same namespace, sections and
variables, so every declaration keeps its name and type). No statement changed. The two
declarations left in the scaffold remainder, which imports this module and
`CausalScaffold.GerochEquiv`, are the only ones that use `theo:geroch`'s cited (iii)⇒(i):
`SingularFlatAxioms.geroch_sing_of_stronglyCausal` and its witness `timelikeLine_geroch_sing`.

> `prop:mesure_admissible`. Let $M$ be a strongly causal $\mass{\geq 0}$-manifold. Then $M$
> carries a measure $\mu_-$ admissible in the past and a measure $\mu_+$ admissible in the future.

> `rem:singular_flat_spacetime_therefore`. A singular flat spacetime is therefore a differential
> manifold and satisfies all the hypotheses of Geroch's Theorem \ref{theo:geroch}.

> `theo:geroch_sing`. Let $M$ be a singular flat spacetime. The following are equivalent:
> (i) $M$ is globally hyperbolic; (ii) $M$ admits a Cauchy time function; (iii) $M$ admits a
> Cauchy hypersurface. Moreover, if $\Sigma$ is a Cauchy surface of $M$, then $M$ is
> homeomorphic to $\Sigma\times \RR$.

> `def:singular_spacetime`. Let $A$ be a subset of $\RR_+$. An $\mass{A}$-spacetime is a
> connected $\E^{1,2}_A$-manifold endowed with the causality generated by its $X_A$-atlas and by
> the causalities of $X$ and of the $(X_\alpha)_{\alpha\geq 0}$.

## Hypothesis checklist

| paper hypothesis | here |
