| `E_{≥0}`-manifold, singular flat spacetime | ⚠ strengthened: `SingularFlatAxioms C sing` |
| — connected (`def:singular_spacetime`) | ⚠ weakened: not used (`SingularFlatSpacetime` carries it) |
| `prop:mesure_admissible`: strongly causal | ⚠ weakened: causal (`IsCausal`); the paper uses strong causality for causally convex charts (l.1736–1745), which `ModelMeasures` carries |
| — (i) of `prop:mesure_dieckmann_topo`: `λ₃`, `λ₃ + λ₁` in causally convex charts (l.1736–1745) | ⚠ strengthened: `ModelMeasures C` |
| `rem:singular_flat_spacetime_therefore`: strongly causal (DEC-18) | ✓ carried (`geroch_hypotheses`); the measures ⚠ strengthened: `ModelMeasures`; without either, every hypothesis of `theo:geroch` but local causal convexity and the measures is proved (`geroch_hypotheses_of_singularFlat`) |
| `theo:geroch_sing`: strongly causal (DEC-18), the equivalence | not here: ✓ carried by `geroch_sing_of_stronglyCausal`, the principal statement, in the scaffold remainder `CausalScaffold.SingularGeroch`, which rests on `theo:geroch`'s cited (iii)⇒(i) |
| — (i)⇒(ii), (i)⇒(iii) | ⚠ weakened: strong causality not used, global hyperbolicity gives it (`geroch_sing_i_imp_ii`, `geroch_sing_i_imp_iii`) |
| — "homeomorphic to `Σ × ℝ`" | ⚠ weakened: causal (`IsCausal`), not strongly causal; ⚠ strengthened: the flow of `lem:vecteur` is the named hypothesis `VecteurFlow C` (`geroch_sing_split`) |
| (ii) "a Cauchy time function" | ⚠ reading: strictly increasing along `≤` (DEC-15) |

## SCOPE (disclosed)

* **`def:singular_spacetime` is abstracted**: no atlas, no model spaces `X`, `X_α`, no generated
  causality. What stands for it is `SingularFlatAxioms C sing` (the causal and topological facts
  Section 3 derives for `E_{≥0}`-manifolds, `Causal.SingularFlat`) plus connectedness,
  `SingularFlatSpacetime`; `A = ℝ₊` is not modelled (the sets `sing α` may be empty).
* **`theo:geroch_sing` is here in part.** (i)⇒(ii), (i)⇒(iii) and the splitting are proved here
  with no `sorry` beneath them. The equivalence `geroch_sing_of_stronglyCausal` (with its witness
  `timelikeLine_geroch_sing`) is in the scaffold remainder: its (iii)⇒(i) is `theo:geroch`'s,
  which the paper cites and `CausalScaffold.GerochEquiv` carries as its one `sorry`.
* **Strong causality is a hypothesis of `theo:geroch_sing` and of
  `rem:singular_flat_spacetime_therefore` (DEC-18), and this finding is why.** `theo:geroch` asks
  `M` locally causally convex (read as strong causality, DEC-7) and a pair of admissible measures;
  `prop:mesure_admissible` gives the measures only for strongly causal `M`, and nothing in
  Section 3 makes a singular flat spacetime strongly causal (l.1216 reads "locally causally
  convex ⇒ strongly causal"). By hand (not formalized: the library has no quotient structure for `E_α` modulo a translation): for `α > 0`,
  `E_α` modulo a translation along its (timelike) singular line is a connected singular flat
  spacetime with a non-empty singular locus, so it does not depend on whether `A = ℝ₊` allows an
  empty one; its singular line closes into a closed timelike curve, it is totally vicious
  (`J^-(q) = M` for every `q`), and it carries no measure admissible in the past (property 3.
  fails). `E^{1,2}` modulo a timelike translation is the same example if an empty singular locus
  is allowed. So the remark, read without strong causality, overclaims, and the proof of
  `theo:geroch_sing` (l.1781–1785) needs it for (ii)⇒(iii) and (iii)⇒(i). Under DEC-18 the
  remark is `geroch_hypotheses`, here, and the theorem is `geroch_sing_of_stronglyCausal`, in the
  scaffold remainder. (i)⇒(ii) and (i)⇒(iii) do not need the hypothesis, global hyperbolicity
  giving strong causality (`prop:GH_fortement_causal`). The form without strong causality is not
  stated.
* **`J^±(p) ≠ {p}`** (l.1783–1785) is proved from the structure, without the paper's
  "3-dimensional `J^+(p)`": `I^±(p)` is non-empty and open (or, at a BTZ point, `J^-(p)`
  accumulates at `p`), and `M` has no isolated point (`Jplus_ne_singleton`,
  `Jminus_ne_singleton`).
* **The splitting `M ≃ Σ × ℝ`** is proved from the named hypothesis `VecteurFlow C`, the flow of
  the `C¹` non-singular future causal vector field of `lem:vecteur` (l.1751–1769, a differentiable
  object the library does not have), with what the proof (l.1787–1796) asserts of it: complete,
  continuous, its orbits inextensible causal curves, each orbit injective when `M` is causal
  (`X` non-singular, so an orbit returning to a point is a closed causal curve; `M` is causal
  under DEC-18, and `geroch_sing_split` asks `IsCausal` only), and `ψ : Σ × ℝ → M` open (the
  `C⁰` content of "a local diffeomorphism"). `VecteurFlow.isOpenMap` is the half of the
  homeomorphism the paper asserts rather than argues (l.1792), so the formal content of
  `geroch_sing_split` is the bijectivity argument: the orbits meet `Σ` exactly once (`Σ` Cauchy,
  the orbits inextensible) and are injective. The structure itself is not used. Without that
  hypothesis the statement for the abstract structure would be stronger than the paper's, which
  claims the splitting for manifolds only, and its truth there is unknown: the counterexample of
  l.1309–1314 (two copies of `ℝ` glued along `ℝ₋`) is non-Hausdorff and excluded by the field
  `t2`, and a Hausdorff Y-tree is not tarentin at its branch point; no counterexample is known.
* **`lem:cup_cap_BTZ` is stated for globally hyperbolic `M` (DEC-19)**, the setting of its only
  use (l.2122); its certificate is `cupCapBTZAsPrinted_of_globallyHyperbolic`. The printed form
  (strong causality only), which is false (`Causal.CupCapBTZCounterexample.not_cupCapBTZAsPrinted`,
  at `E₀` minus a point of its BTZ line), is not asserted: it stays the `Prop`
  `CupCapBTZAsPrinted C sing`, with that finding.
* **The BTZ facts are fields** (`Causal.SingularFlat`, SCOPE): the full structure with
  `sing 0 ≠ ∅` has the witness `E₀` (`Causal.E0.singularFlatAxioms`), and every Hausdorff, second
  countable `E_{≥0}`-manifold satisfies it (`Causal.SFAManifolds.singularFlatAxioms`). Its former field `Iplus_eq`
  (`I^+(p) = J^+(p) ∖ sing_0`, flagged at l.1351 as asserted without proof) is **false in `E₀`**
  (the radial null ray) and was replaced by `Iplus_of_lt` (DEC-64, true in `E₀`); `K_monotone`,
  through which `mesure_admissible` and every theorem here using it pass, is re-proved from the
  corrected field with its statement unchanged. `SingularFlatSpacetime` extends the corrected
  bundle, so no statement here changed.
* **Satisfiability.** The timelike line (no singular point, the standard Gaussian measure in the
  chart `ℝ`, the flow `(x, t) ↦ x + t`) satisfies `SingularFlatSpacetime`, `ModelMeasures`,
  strong causality and `VecteurFlow` (`timelikeLine_singularFlatSpacetime`,
  `timelikeLine_modelMeasures`, `timelikeLine_vecteurFlow`); `mesure_admissible`,
  `geroch_hypotheses`, `geroch_sing_i_imp_ii`, `geroch_sing_i_imp_iii`, `geroch_sing_split` and
